## Scope

Confirm only the actual published range or inequality assertion, preserving
open/closed bounds and the target object, collection, or extrema. Distinguish
assertion confirmation from an exact numerical-statistic match in evidence and
counts. Unknown inclusivity or source meaning cannot be guessed. A collection
claim is not established by cherry-picking one member; interval objects and
reported endpoint statistics must retain the actual source assertion/target.
Do not fabricate a midpoint, widen tolerance, hide required comparisons, promote
canonical categories, or silently rescore legacy cases.

